  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"By Amy Borezo, with Lecture on moving by Yvonne Rainer, reprinted with permission of the author, originally published in Aspen magazine, 1971 ... Images inspired by the work of Frank and Lillian Gilbreth who developed time and motion studies in the early 20th c. to improve worker efficiency and productivity"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">"Printed and bound by the artist in Hanover, NH, and Orange, MA, in the fall of 2011 and winter of 2012. Hand-set metal and wood type, body text in Palatino"--Colophon.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">The illustrations are tracings of the movements of seven construction workers from a motion study video produced by the Gilbreths, printed in silver and black. Cf. Vamp &amp; Tramp Booksellers website.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">An accordion-style binding with each double leaf sewn into a mountain fold. The edge of the top leaf is labeled "pull." When fully extended the book measures 158 cm.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
